cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SSG — Static Site Generator"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "SSG Contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/static-site-generator"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/static-site-generator"
url: "https://static-site-generator.com"
abstract: >-
  A secure-by-default static site generator built in Rust, with WCAG 2.2
  AA validation, CSP/SRI hardening, native JS/CSS minification,
  automated CycloneDX SBOM generation, a local LLM content pipeline, a
  WebAssembly target, interactive islands, streaming compilation for
  100K+ pages, 28-locale internationalisation, and one-command
  deployment. Validation runs inside the build rather than after it, so
  a page that fails an accessibility, security or metadata check is
  reported with its file and line during compilation.
keywords:
  - static-site-generator
  - rust
  - accessibility
  - wcag
  - web-performance
  - security
  - webassembly
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
version: 0.0.60
date-released: "2026-09-09"
